gaqn(){return"Switch between Team view \u2014 the schedule of everyone who reports to you \u2014 and Colleagues view, where you draft your own shifts alongside your peers."},
gaZR(){return"Schedule Views"},
gaZQ(){return"Look at the same week four ways: Weekly grid, a Daily timeline, a Monthly calendar, and My Schedule for your own shifts."},
gaq4(){return"Navigate & Filter"},
gaq3(){return"Use Today and the arrows to move between weeks, then narrow the team by department, location, or reporting scope (direct, indirect, or both)."},
gaq2(){return"Copy Last Week"},
gaq1(){return"Reuse last week's plan in one step \u2014 it copies shifts into any empty days for the current week, skipping days that are already filled."},
gaqg(){return"Publish the Week"},
gaqf(){return"Turn your drafts into the official schedule. Once every cell is filled the button turns blue; publishing notifies the affected employees. It stays disabled while empty cells remain."},
gaZw(){return"Week at a Glance"},
gaZu(){return"Live totals for the visible team: people scheduled, shifts this week, conflicts, unpublished drafts, and how many are on approved leave."},
gaZz(){return"Colour Legend"},
gaZx(){return"What the cell colours mean \u2014 Morning, Afternoon, Night and Overnight shifts, plus Leave and Day-off, and the markers for drafts and conflicts."},
gaq0(){return"Assign a Shift"},
gaq_(){return"Tap any empty cell to open the shift editor and set the times, or tap an existing shift to edit it. Conflicts (rest gaps, leave overlaps) are flagged automatically."},
gaqe(){return"Select Multiple Cells"},
gaqd(){return"Need the same shift across several people or days? Drag across the grid \u2014 or long-press then tap \u2014 to select many cells, then assign them all at once from the bar that appears."},
gaqm(){return"Reusable Templates"},
gaql(){return"In the shift editor, tick 'Save as template' and give it a name to store a shift you use often. Next time it appears as a chip you can apply in one tap."},
gaqk(){return"Swaps, Conflicts & Time Off"},
gaqj(){return"The side panel collects swap requests to approve or decline, scheduling conflicts to resolve, and your team's approved time off \u2014 all in one place."},
gaZY(){return"Team view tour"},
gaZ3(){return"Colleagues view tour"},
gaZT(){return"Navigate Weeks"},
gaZS(){return"Use Today and the arrows to move between weeks. The week label shows which week you're viewing."},
gaZP(){return"Your Draft Actions"},
gaZO(){return"In Colleagues view you draft your own row. 'Copy last week' fills your empty days from last week, and the amber hint reminds you that your manager publishes your final schedule."},
gaqi(){return"Draft Your Own Shifts"},
gaqh(){return"Tap an empty day on your row to propose a shift, or tap your own draft to edit it. Days your manager has reserved show a lock and can't be edited. Your drafts stay pending until your manager publishes them."},
ga8B(){return"Request a Swap"},
ga8A(){return"Tap a colleague's shift to request a swap with them. You can only swap future shifts, and not when either of you is on leave or already has an open request for that day."},
gaZN(){return"Manager Comparison Row"},
gaZM(){return"This pinned row shows your manager's schedule for reference (read-only, marked with a 'Manager' badge) so you can line your own shifts up against theirs."},
gaZL(){return"Pick a Week"},
gaZK(){return"Tap the arrows to move between weeks; the label in the middle shows the week you're viewing."},
gaZF(){return"Week at a Glance"},
gaZE(){return"Quick totals for the week: people scheduled and shifts always show; in Team view you also see conflicts and unpublished drafts."},
gaZB(){return"Choose a Day"},
gaZA(){return"Tap a day to focus the list below on that day's shifts. Swipe the strip sideways to reach the whole week."},
gaq6(){return"Bulk Assign Shifts"},
gaq5(){return"Tap 'Assign shifts\u2026' to open the bulk sheet and give the same shift to several people across several days at once \u2014 it walks you through the shift (template or custom times), the days, then who it applies to. The 'Fill this day' link above the list does the same for just the day you're viewing."},
gaZJ(){return"Schedule Views"},
gaZI(){return"Swipe the tab strip to move between views: Weekly (the day-by-day list below), Monthly for a whole-month overview, On Shift Now for who's working right now, My Schedule for your own shifts, and Swaps \u2014 its badge counts requests waiting on you. Managers also get a More tab for publishing and copying."},
gaq8(){return"Filter the Team"},
gaq7(){return"Tap this chip to open the filters sheet, then narrow the list by department, location, or reporting scope. Nothing changes until you tap Apply, and Reset clears everything. The chip itself shows what's currently applied."},
gaZD(){return"Your Shift Actions"},
gaZC(){return"'Copy last week' fills your empty days from last week, and 'Assign shifts\u2026' opens a sheet locked to your own row so you can draft several days at once. Your drafts stay pending until your manager publishes them."},
gaqc(){return"Approve Swap Requests"},
gaqb(){return"Swap requests from your team land here under 'Pending action'. Each card shows both shifts side by side so you can compare them, then Approve or Decline. The tab badge tells you how many are waiting."},
gaZH(){return"Your Swaps"},
gaZG(){return"Everything about your swaps in one tab: requests colleagues sent you (accept or decline), the ones you've sent (which you can cancel), and your past swap history. To start a new one, tap a colleague's shift in Weekly or use 'Swap with' in My Schedule."},
gaqa(){return"Publish & Copy"},
gaq9(){return"The manager actions live here. 'Publish week' turns your drafts into the official schedule and notifies everyone affected \u2014 it stays disabled until every cell is filled. 'Copy last week' reuses last week's plan for any empty days."},
gaZv(){return"Totals for the week you're viewing: how many people are scheduled and how many shifts there are in total."},
gaZy(){return"What the colours mean \u2014 Morning, Afternoon, Night and Overnight shifts, plus Leave and Day-off."},
